In simple words, Section 164 of the Code of Criminal Procedure, 1973 deals with Recording of confessions and statements. When a confession is made before a Magistrate, the Magistrate shall, if the person making the confession appears or is brought before him, examine the person making the confession as to the facts stated in the confession, and may, if necessary, put any question or questions to him for the purpose of discovering the truth;
Provided that no person shall be convicted of any offence on the basis of a confession made to a police officer, unless the Magistrate or police officer, as the case may be, has recorded the confession and the person making the confession has been duly cautioned to attend the Magistrate or police officer and to make a true statement of the facts;
